steps.prompt:
Feature request: {{feature}}
Run label: {{run_label}}

Write the requirements to docs/requirements/{{run_label}}.md and the architecture to docs/architecture/{{run_label}}.md. Add an ADR under docs/adr/ only if an architectural decision changes. Mark every open decision from structure.md as 'needs human decision'; do not resolve it.

Assign exactly one implementation agent using this mapping: Web Audio, equalizer, analysis -> audio-engineer; main process, preload, IPC contracts, build config, package.json -> desktop-engineer; renderer UI, stores, skin loader -> frontend-engineer; GitHub features -> github-engineer; skin art, icons -> art-director; packaging, CI -> release-engineer. If the feature spans several domains, recommend splitting it into separate runs and assign only the first slice.

Do not edit source, run commands, commit or push. Final response: a short summary, the two file paths, and a last line exactly 'DOMAIN AGENT: <agent-name>'.

Human approval gate before implementation. Read {{artifacts.requirements}} and {{artifacts.architecture}}. Proposed assignment from the previous step:

{{requirements-architecture.output}}

Call send_message with severity warning, summarizing scope, risks, open decisions and the proposed DOMAIN AGENT, and ask the human to approve, change the domain agent, or reject. Wait for the answer. Do not edit any file. If the human rejects, call send_message with severity error. If the human approves, call send_message with severity success. Final response: a last line exactly 'APPROVED DOMAIN AGENT: <agent-name>' with the agent the human approved.
